# Keep LF in everything bash has to read.
#
# A CRLF shell script or env file usually appears to work on Windows, because
# Git Bash's /etc/profile enables `igncr` and so strips the carriage returns for
# you. A bash spawned by something else -- a Python subprocess, a hook, CI --
# reads no profile, has igncr off, and then a line containing only "\r" is a
# command: `./.env: line 3: $'\r': command not found`. Under `set -e` that
# aborts the whole script, and the error names a file and line that look fine in
# an editor.
#
# This is how .env.example and tools/certs/make-ca.sh ended up with CRLF while
# `./fc.sh` still worked by hand and failed the moment fleetctl.py invoked it.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf
*.sql     text eol=lf
*.env     text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf

# Container images are built from these; the shell inside is Linux.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
